MDL113, F1, F12: mydumper v0.19.1-x has no config pre-processor: it hands the
file to g_key_file_load_from_file as it is. A valueless flag ("routines")
is then not a key/value pair, so GLib rejects the file and mydumper ignores
all of it: it logs "Failed to load config file", runs with its defaults (no
routines, users.email in plaintext), connects through [client] and exits 0.
From v0.19.3-1 the pre-processor turns the same line into "routines= 1"
(mdl308-bare-flag-accepted-from-v0.19.3). With the default matrix, this
scenario runs on the newest v0.19.1-x image.
-- scenario --
tool: mydumper
versions: < v0.19.3-1
args: --defaults-file /work/defaults.cnf --database app
lint: MDL113, MDL405
expect config-loaded: false
expect stderr-contains: Failed to load config file /work/defaults.cnf
expect exit: 0
expect connected: true
expect routines-dumped: false
expect column app.users.email: plaintext
-- defaults.cnf --
[client]
host=mysql
user=e2e
password=e2e-password

[mydumper]
routines
threads=2

[`app`.`users`]
`email`=random_string
